hi i'm shannon from khan academy and i  want to show you how to make the most of  your learning time on official sat  practice  research has shown that more time spent  on official sat practice is associated  with greater sat scores  but how you spend that time really  matters  before we begin let's make sure you know  how to access official sat practice  make sure you're signed into your khan  academy account by checking for your  name in the upper right hand corner  if you're using official sct practice in  a class you should see a tab that says  sat on the left side navigation  select the sat tab  from there select practice to be taken  to your student dashboard  if you aren't using sat practice in a  class you can select edit courses to add  the sat tab to your khan academy account  number one  link your account to college board  to receive a personalized practice plan  you have two options  number one take a series of diagnostic  quizzes  or number two  link your college board account to khan  academy  the easiest way to get a study plan that  is personalized to your results is to  link your con and college board accounts  once your accounts are linked we'll  automatically recommend skills where you  have room to improve  especially ones that show up frequently  on the sat  we recommend that you link your accounts  so you can waste no time improving the  right skills  number two  follow your personalized practice  recommendations if you have already  linked your khan academy in college  board accounts you will see your skill  recommendations on the practice tab  at the top of the page you should see a  set of recommended practice for math and  reading and writing that always end in a  timed mini section  now let's take a deeper look at how  skills are recommended  let's say there are two skills at two  different levels skill a  is at level two  skill b is at level three  you might think it would be more  important to improve skill a  however in some cases we may recommend  that you practice skill b because it  shows up more frequently on the sat  and it proving it to level four would do  more to raise your score  number three  level up skills  in official sat practice you have a  specific skill level for the 41 skills  and math and the 28 skills in reading  and writing  as you answer questions your skill  levels will move up  or down depending on how you do  leveling up your skills shows you that  you are consistently advancing in the  content on the sat and it's a great way  to monitor your progress  you might be wondering  but what if i do if i get stuck on a  skill  it's normal to feel stuck at times when  studying for the sat we've all been  there  but those moments of confusion are also  the times when you have the opportunity  to improve your score the most  push through by using the hints  instructional videos  or ask for help when you're learning a  new skill  as you answer questions on official sat  practice you have access to text  explanations and videos to deepen your  understanding of the content  you can also use the review tab to  review your answers from completed  practice  if you're still stuck reach out to one  of your classmates a teacher or a family  member for support  number four  take a full length practice test  select the full test tab at the top to  access the full length sat practice test  taking a practice test is a crucial step  to ensure you're prepared for a test day  by simulating the real test experience  eight full-length practice tests are  available on official sat practice which  can be taken in one sitting or section  by section over time  the information from your full-length  test will also result in even more  personalized practice  now that you know the top four tips to  using official sat practice you're ready  to get started  log in to your khan academy account  today happy studying
 

